From ba4bc23f91964e6be5342c1b2be9700cb300749c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:37:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Derive discrete cash-flow quarters from cumulative
 figures; TTM growth needs a positive base

Interim cash-flow statements are cumulative from the start of the fiscal year, so quarter-on-quarter changes and
trailing-twelve-month sums of operating cash flow, capex and free cash flow had no discrete quarters to work from.
A discrete quarter of operating cash flow or capex is now the difference of two cumulative figures with the same
start that end one quarter apart (Q1 or YTD, YTD or FY). A reported quarter is never replaced, a gap is never
bridged, and a quarter derived earlier is recomputed from the current cumulative figures rather than treated as
reported. Income-statement lines are not derived (IFRS 5 re-presents them between filings; cash-flow totals
include discontinued operations).

Trailing-twelve-month growth is no longer emitted on a non-positive prior window, the rule quarter-on-quarter
changes already follow.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CfTpoii6QDStyTPdotmEdY
