From 3563927ea020d26c1e2a2ed38cbab8d9474ff797 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:37:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Recompute derived quarters and free cash flow at build
 end; refresh calculated rows on restated inputs

Free cash flow and derived quarters often combine figures from different filings, so a later restatement of one
input (SABIC's FY2025 capex completed with intangible additions) left the calculated row, and every ratio computed
from it, current with a value no current input supports. The build-end reconciliation now recomputes derived
cash-flow quarters and calculated free cash flow first and feeds them to the comparison pass, and then refreshes
every other calculated row whose formula gives another value on the current inputs. A refresh only corrects a
value: it never adds or withdraws a row, and a formula combining two or more re-presented lines from different
filings is left as computed within its filing.

Across the 37-company build, calculated rows that disagree with their recomputation fall from 31 to 16 (the rest
are single-filing margins kept on purpose, and rows computed outside the calculator).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CfTpoii6QDStyTPdotmEdY
